WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.830
I asked a helper to plan our

2
00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:02.990
class trip to Dala.

3
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.360
It messaged all your families

4
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.960
before it even knew the way!

5
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.640
The steps were in the wrong order.

6
00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:11.410
Let’s fix that.

7
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.680
Today: big jobs, in small steps.

8
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.350
Big jobs are made of small steps,

9
00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.550
and a plan puts them in order.

10
00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.850
To plan a trip, first find the way.

11
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.700
Then check the weather.

12
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:28.610
Then tell the families.

13
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.220
The order matters.

14
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.900
You put on your socks before

15
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.620
your shoes, not after!

16
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.240
A helper needs the right order

17
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.220
too, or the job goes wrong.

18
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.060
I asked Darsi Tiny how far it is

19
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.500
from Kafi to Dala, and what the

20
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.640
weather is there tomorrow.

21
00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.010
Its plan: first the route,

22
00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.110
then the weather.

23
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.080
Seventy kilometres, and partly cloudy!

24
00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.160
Sometimes a step needs the

25
00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.660
answer from the step before.

26
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.500
Ask: what is 6B’s first lesson tomorrow,

27
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.920
and remind me at half past seven.

28
00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.750
The timetable says PE, so the

29
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.050
reminder says: 6B, PE.

30
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:12.800
Quick check!

31
00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.820
To plan the trip, which step must

32
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.240
come before telling the families?

33
00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:20.630
Find the way and check the weather.

34
00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:22.900
Only tell the families when

35
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.060
you know the plan works.

36
00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.970
Find out first, then act!

37
00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.120
But steps can go wrong.

38
00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.680
On Saturday, the timetable

39
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.060
tool said: no school.

40
00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.710
Darsi Tiny still set a

41
00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:38.430
reminder that made no sense!

42
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.620
A good helper stops and checks.

43
00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:44.950
In the app, guess the plan first:

44
00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.370
which tools, in which order?

45
00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.060
Then watch Darsi Tiny do it.

46
00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.850
Try Saturday too, and see what happens.

47
00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:54.670
Your turn.

48
00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.340
The timetable tool says: no

49
00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.340
school on Saturday.

50
00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:00.340
What should the helper do next?

51
00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:02.880
Stop and tell you.

52
00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:06.000
Remember: big jobs are small

53
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.420
steps, and the order matters.

54
00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.240
One step’s answer can help the next.

55
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.380
And when a step goes

56
00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.200
wrong, stop and check.

57
00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:18.870
Try it yourself: write the steps for

58
00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:21.490
making tea on small cards, and mix them

59
00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:21.630
up.

60
00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:24.410
Ask someone at home to put them in order.

61
00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.780
Which steps must come first?
